    "created_at": "2017-01-03T08:20:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-03T08:20:35Z",
    "body": "I believe Bikeshed's \"abstract-op\" basically just means to make the name case sensitive; as opposed to the `dfn` type that can be used with any case when referencing. So it's different from JS \"Abstract Operation\" concept.\r\n\r\nIf you have multiple terms with the same name and type, you can disambiguate them using `for` typically, or convince @tabatkins to add more types for JS concepts.\r\n\r\nhttps://tabatkins.github.io/bikeshed/#dfn-types",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/270067382/reactions",
